WEBVTT

00:00:02.020 --> 00:00:03.230
Hurry!

00:00:05.020 --> 00:00:07.480
Non sia cosi! Naoto!

00:00:07.860 --> 00:00:12.150
Naoto, don't get yourself
hurt just for my sake!

00:00:13.820 --> 00:00:14.910
Thanks.

00:00:15.410 --> 00:00:16.950
But don't worry.

00:00:18.910 --> 00:00:21.160
What're you just standing around for?

00:00:40.640 --> 00:00:41.640
Sakurai!

00:00:54.150 --> 00:00:55.070
Yo!

00:00:55.070 --> 00:00:57.280
Sorry I took so long, Deputy!

00:00:57.280 --> 00:00:59.080
Last guy taken care of!

00:00:59.490 --> 00:01:02.040
Iwaizumi! You saved us!

00:01:02.580 --> 00:01:03.960
Thank you too, Sakurai.

00:01:03.960 --> 00:01:08.710
I told you, I'll protect you.

00:02:43.550 --> 00:02:46.640
I see. You took the Tohoku Bullet Train!

00:02:46.640 --> 00:02:48.850
I asked Ms. Iida,

00:02:48.850 --> 00:02:53.560
and she told me transferring to the bullet train at Omiya would get me to Sendai ahead of you guys.

00:02:53.560 --> 00:02:56.530
The Hokutosei doesn't have a very high top speed, after all.

00:02:57.400 --> 00:02:59.400
Sorry you got mixed up in this.

00:02:59.400 --> 00:03:02.450
Geez, you really pulled some crazy stunts.

00:03:02.450 --> 00:03:04.490
Don't make me worry like that.

00:03:04.910 --> 00:03:06.950
You too, Sakurai. Got that?

00:03:07.450 --> 00:03:09.460
S-Sure.

00:03:09.460 --> 00:03:10.210
All right!

00:03:10.830 --> 00:03:14.920
I tied up our two captives and stuffed them in the luggage compartment like you asked.

00:03:15.290 --> 00:03:17.590
What're we gonna do with them?

00:03:17.590 --> 00:03:21.260
We'll hand them over to the PSF at Hakodate Station once we arrive.

00:03:21.260 --> 00:03:23.180
Roger that, Deputy!

00:03:23.180 --> 00:03:27.270
Before we do, I gotta give
them one good punch.

00:03:27.270 --> 00:03:28.680
Sakurai.

00:03:32.810 --> 00:03:33.980
Koumi?

00:03:33.980 --> 00:03:36.230
So that's this girl's name, huh?

00:03:37.900 --> 00:03:44.120
Tokyo Central Railroad Public Security Force, Fourth Peacekeeper Squad, Haruka Koumi.

00:03:45.030 --> 00:03:46.330
That sound right?

00:03:46.330 --> 00:03:47.410
Koumi?

00:03:47.410 --> 00:03:48.540
Are you there?

00:03:49.580 --> 00:03:50.870
Who are you?

00:03:50.870 --> 00:03:54.630
Imagine my surprise when it was just a dummy in the prince's room.

00:03:54.630 --> 00:03:56.920
The best laid plans, no?

00:03:56.920 --> 00:03:58.880
Prince? You mean Bernina?

00:03:59.380 --> 00:04:02.510
So now this girl will be my hostage.

00:04:03.090 --> 00:04:06.760
Naturally, I'll trade her for the prince.

00:04:07.930 --> 00:04:10.850
Not happening. We don't
negotiate with terrorists.

00:04:10.850 --> 00:04:15.230
If my hostage is useless, I'll just have to find another use for her.

00:04:15.230 --> 00:04:16.480
No, don't!

00:04:16.480 --> 00:04:20.150
Give up on trying to find us.

00:04:20.150 --> 00:04:24.490
You try anything funny,
and the girl gets it.

00:04:24.910 --> 00:04:26.200
I'll contact you again.

00:04:26.200 --> 00:04:27.240
Hold on a second!

00:04:34.040 --> 00:04:37.630
When I knocked on her door and
no one answered, I just ignored it.

00:04:38.210 --> 00:04:39.340
This is all my fault.

00:04:40.300 --> 00:04:43.050
She was definitely attacked here.

00:04:43.380 --> 00:04:45.550
No evidence left by the criminal, though.

00:04:46.010 --> 00:04:47.350
There has to be something!

00:04:47.350 --> 00:04:48.470
Anything!

00:04:50.680 --> 00:04:51.810
Takayama.

00:04:51.810 --> 00:04:56.310
Times like this, the Deputy <i>has</i> to keep calm when making decisions.

00:04:58.610 --> 00:05:00.320
We're on a moving train.

00:05:00.320 --> 00:05:02.570
There are only so many places he can hide.

00:05:02.570 --> 00:05:04.570
If we search every inch of this train...

00:05:04.570 --> 00:05:06.610
Backup's going to take some time.

00:05:06.610 --> 00:05:12.580
I called HQ, but for things like this they prefer to not make any sudden moves.

00:05:12.580 --> 00:05:17.580
Chief Ominato also refuses to take action until the situation is clear.

00:05:18.250 --> 00:05:22.340
You're right that this might be a move to decrease the prince's security.

00:05:23.300 --> 00:05:28.340
As long as we don't know how many of them there are,
moving around recklessly can't be a good idea.

00:05:28.340 --> 00:05:30.350
Just hang on for a little longer.

00:05:30.850 --> 00:05:32.810
I'm coming to you.

00:05:32.810 --> 00:05:39.190
I'll also contact the conductor and
ask him to handle the other passengers.

00:05:39.190 --> 00:05:42.190
M-Ms. Iida, I...

00:05:42.190 --> 00:05:43.570
Don't worry.

00:05:43.570 --> 00:05:46.780
You'll make the right choice. I know it.

00:05:48.240 --> 00:05:51.370
You're such a limp noodle, Takayama.

00:05:51.370 --> 00:05:54.580
I-I'm worried, all right?
Think about the situation!

00:05:54.580 --> 00:05:58.750
That doesn't mean you have to go running to someone else for every little thing.

00:05:58.750 --> 00:06:00.960
Well, aren't <i>you</i> calm, Sakurai?

00:06:01.420 --> 00:06:03.550
Every second we waste, KoumiвЂ”

00:06:04.170 --> 00:06:07.840
Haruka might be a student OJT, but she's still a PSF member.

00:06:08.180 --> 00:06:10.470
She can take care of herself.

00:06:10.470 --> 00:06:13.680
She's not strong like you are, Sakurai!

00:06:13.680 --> 00:06:16.810
All right, stop. That's enough.

00:06:17.890 --> 00:06:20.270
I'm pretty sweaty.

00:06:20.270 --> 00:06:22.980
I need to take a shower and refresh.

00:06:22.980 --> 00:06:24.900
Sakurai, come with?

00:06:30.410 --> 00:06:31.950
Thanks for letting me go first.

00:06:31.950 --> 00:06:34.580
Oh, do you know how to use these showers?

00:06:34.580 --> 00:06:37.160
You've got ten minutes of hot or cold water.

00:06:37.160 --> 00:06:38.660
If you take longer than that...

00:06:40.790 --> 00:06:44.000
use this and you can reset the time.

00:06:46.130 --> 00:06:47.840
Thanks for earlier.

00:06:47.840 --> 00:06:49.510
I needed to cool my head.

00:06:49.930 --> 00:06:52.510
Koumi's a good friend of yours, no?

00:06:52.510 --> 00:06:56.270
You be on your guard too, Sasshou. The enemy's seen you with us.

00:06:56.270 --> 00:06:58.020
They might attack you if we get separated.

00:07:00.020 --> 00:07:03.060
So stick with your prince.

00:07:03.560 --> 00:07:05.820
I'm sure he'll protect you.

00:07:07.900 --> 00:07:09.280
My prince?

00:07:13.570 --> 00:07:14.490
What?

00:07:15.530 --> 00:07:16.990
Oh, just thinking.

00:07:16.990 --> 00:07:26.960
Like if you actually end up in the PSF, I hope you get partnered up with someone like Sakurai.

00:07:27.550 --> 00:07:28.840
Don't jinx it!

00:07:28.840 --> 00:07:30.470
I'm gonna be a train driver!

00:07:30.800 --> 00:07:33.140
Safety always comes first!

00:07:33.140 --> 00:07:37.470
Right. Yeah, your dreams are important.

00:07:45.900 --> 00:07:48.690
I thought we weren't stopping until Hakodate.

00:07:48.690 --> 00:07:51.860
We might be stopped,
but we can't get off.

00:07:51.860 --> 00:07:56.160
We're here to switch in
an ED79 electric locomotive.

00:07:56.160 --> 00:07:57.830
ED79?

00:07:57.830 --> 00:07:58.700
Yeah.

00:07:58.700 --> 00:08:03.710
It's equipped with a safety control system to help us get through the Seikan Tunnel.

00:08:03.710 --> 00:08:07.750
It'll pull the Hokutosei all the way to Hakodate.

00:08:19.720 --> 00:08:21.890
Things go okay with you and Sasshou?

00:08:21.890 --> 00:08:23.310
Yeah.

00:08:23.810 --> 00:08:26.520
But "prince" might have been a little overkill.

00:08:26.520 --> 00:08:28.650
Prince? Me?

00:08:28.980 --> 00:08:30.900
What a terrible joke.

00:08:30.900 --> 00:08:32.530
I'm no prince.

00:08:34.570 --> 00:08:36.070
Me, a prince?

00:08:41.700 --> 00:08:43.250
We'll make the trade.

00:08:44.000 --> 00:08:45.750
I've got an idea.

00:08:45.750 --> 00:08:47.420
I'm done changing, Naoto.

00:08:56.970 --> 00:08:59.050
Thank you for riding with us.

00:08:59.560 --> 00:09:01.970
We will soon be stopping at Hakodate.

00:09:01.970 --> 00:09:05.270
The doors will open on the left.
We are stopping on track eight.

00:09:05.270 --> 00:09:09.520
There will be a nine-minute stop as we change engines.

00:09:09.520 --> 00:09:09.730
We're going into the non-electrified zone now.

00:09:09.730 --> 00:09:12.030
The train will leave the station at 6:43 a.m.

00:09:12.030 --> 00:09:13.150
Yeah.

00:09:13.150 --> 00:09:17.160
It's time for the DF51 narrow-gauge diesel engine.

00:09:18.660 --> 00:09:20.910
Time for you too, Takayama.

00:09:22.080 --> 00:09:24.370
So backup didn't arrive, huh?

00:09:26.000 --> 00:09:27.630
No other choice, then.

00:09:35.300 --> 00:09:36.430
Your Highness.

00:09:36.430 --> 00:09:39.140
Ms. Iida will be escorting
Bernina to his destination.

00:09:39.970 --> 00:09:43.020
Now we just have to save Koumi!

00:09:50.400 --> 00:09:52.820
We can only hope they're fooled.

00:09:54.570 --> 00:09:56.150
I think we'll be fine.

00:09:56.700 --> 00:10:01.780
Attacking all-out in a tight space with no way out is a sign they aren't pros.

00:10:02.330 --> 00:10:06.080
They might be strong, but they're like a bunch of street punks.

00:10:06.580 --> 00:10:07.620
I see.

00:10:07.620 --> 00:10:10.670
You've actually got brains
in your skull, Iwaizumi.

00:10:10.670 --> 00:10:13.340
Aw, stop it.

00:10:13.340 --> 00:10:14.380
I'm blushing.

00:10:19.640 --> 00:10:23.350
You read the article about how my four
family members had an accident, right?

00:10:23.930 --> 00:10:29.350
I'm fifth in line to the throne,
but that's only as long as they're alive.

00:10:30.860 --> 00:10:32.570
And if I die,

00:10:34.400 --> 00:10:39.990
that means it's someone sixth in line or lower who hired them.

00:10:41.240 --> 00:10:44.700
Then that's even more reason to not hand you over to them.

00:10:45.870 --> 00:10:48.000
You're a JNR customer.

00:10:49.830 --> 00:10:53.750
It's our job to make sure
you enjoy your journey.

00:10:54.340 --> 00:11:00.220
And if someone wants to get in the way of that, no matter the reason, we have to fight back.

00:11:03.350 --> 00:11:05.350
It makes me happy you'd say that.

00:11:07.100 --> 00:11:10.140
Not exactly what I was
hoping to hear, though.

00:11:12.190 --> 00:11:13.230
Bernina.

00:11:16.940 --> 00:11:19.860
These motherless fucks would kill children.

00:11:19.860 --> 00:11:21.820
I'm out for blood, Deputy.

00:11:21.820 --> 00:11:25.330
You're okay with me shooting
to kill, right, Takayama?

00:11:30.790 --> 00:11:32.250
Thanks for waiting.

00:11:32.250 --> 00:11:34.210
Here are the details for the exchange.

00:11:34.210 --> 00:11:39.630
When we arrive at Datemonbetsu Station,
bring the prince to the diesel engine lead car.

00:11:39.630 --> 00:11:42.720
Only the woman is allowed to be with him.

00:11:52.940 --> 00:11:55.270
Iwaizumi was right.

00:11:55.270 --> 00:11:59.230
Any man who'd insist on a woman for an exchange has no balls.

00:11:59.230 --> 00:12:00.610
Get off!

00:12:06.080 --> 00:12:07.280
Those bastards!

00:12:07.280 --> 00:12:09.540
Bring the prince here.

00:12:09.540 --> 00:12:12.370
Give us Haruka first!

00:12:12.370 --> 00:12:13.580
Look up.

00:12:22.050 --> 00:12:22.930
Haruka.

00:12:22.930 --> 00:12:24.680
The prince. Now.

00:12:24.680 --> 00:12:25.760
Koumi!

00:12:29.850 --> 00:12:30.930
It's not him.

00:12:30.930 --> 00:12:31.810
It's not the prince!

00:12:38.110 --> 00:12:39.400
Takayama!

00:12:41.360 --> 00:12:42.820
Boo-yah!

00:12:47.870 --> 00:12:49.450
Koumi, are you okay?

00:12:50.410 --> 00:12:51.700
Takayama...

00:12:53.120 --> 00:12:54.960
Takayama!

00:13:02.800 --> 00:13:04.840
This is bad. We have to stop the train.

00:13:04.840 --> 00:13:07.090
Or else everyone on this train is in trouble!

00:13:08.010 --> 00:13:09.680
But what can we do?

00:13:11.270 --> 00:13:12.220
Well?

00:13:12.220 --> 00:13:14.060
Anything?

00:13:15.440 --> 00:13:18.360
We have to control the train from the driver's seat in the lead car.

00:13:29.830 --> 00:13:32.120
They're holed up in there.
This'll be difficult.

00:13:32.750 --> 00:13:35.370
Takayama, where's the tear gas?

00:13:35.370 --> 00:13:37.290
Trains aren't stocked with that!

00:13:37.290 --> 00:13:39.000
There'd only be flares...

00:13:39.590 --> 00:13:42.590
Oh! Signal flares!

00:13:42.590 --> 00:13:43.630
Signal flares?

00:13:44.800 --> 00:13:48.970
Koumi, do you know where the signal flares are kept in a DF51?

00:13:52.890 --> 00:13:55.390
I remember reading
the manual during training.

00:13:55.850 --> 00:14:00.770
Look. There are pipe-looking things sticking out above the driver's seat.

00:14:03.150 --> 00:14:05.110
So shoot that, right?

00:14:05.490 --> 00:14:06.610
Leave it to me!

00:14:06.610 --> 00:14:07.450
Okay!

00:14:07.450 --> 00:14:08.860
I'll draw their fire!

00:14:10.990 --> 00:14:12.740
H-Hey, Sakurai!

00:14:14.120 --> 00:14:15.250
Be careful.

00:14:16.370 --> 00:14:18.080
Trust me.

00:14:45.190 --> 00:14:48.320
Hey, we're going really fast.

00:14:48.950 --> 00:14:51.570
It's okay. I'll slow us down.

00:14:55.700 --> 00:14:58.580
We're almost at the next station, Higashimuroran.

00:15:00.870 --> 00:15:02.710
It's no use! It's not responding!

00:15:02.710 --> 00:15:05.170
Try putting the reverser in neutral!

00:15:05.170 --> 00:15:06.210
The reverser?

00:15:06.210 --> 00:15:08.550
It's like a clutch on a manual car.

00:15:08.550 --> 00:15:13.010
You press the button and then switch
between forward, neutral, and reverse.

00:15:13.010 --> 00:15:16.270
If you put it in neutral, the power transmission will be cut.

00:15:16.720 --> 00:15:19.230
There. The button right in front of you.

00:15:25.820 --> 00:15:29.900
It's not working! The control system must have been broken!

00:15:29.900 --> 00:15:31.740
In all that gunfire...

00:15:34.780 --> 00:15:36.910
We'll just have to brake at speed!

00:15:36.910 --> 00:15:38.160
Grab on to something!

00:15:42.290 --> 00:15:44.080
Damn! No response?

00:15:44.420 --> 00:15:46.300
Try the independent brake!

00:15:46.300 --> 00:15:50.170
If that's not working either, push both
all the way in for an emergency braking!

00:15:57.970 --> 00:15:59.600
The ATS isn't working either!

00:16:03.900 --> 00:16:04.980
Takayama?

00:16:06.860 --> 00:16:08.650
We have to detach the engines.

00:16:09.230 --> 00:16:10.740
What?!

00:16:10.740 --> 00:16:13.860
It's these two cars that are out of control.

00:16:13.860 --> 00:16:16.450
If we detach them, that should save the passenger cars!

00:16:16.870 --> 00:16:18.240
But we're at top speed!

00:16:18.240 --> 00:16:19.660
We don't have a choice!

00:16:20.160 --> 00:16:24.120
It's our job to protect
our customers, no matter what.

00:16:32.340 --> 00:16:33.130
There you go.

00:16:33.130 --> 00:16:34.050
That's the way.

00:16:38.350 --> 00:16:41.680
Iwaizumi, keep an eye on those captives till we can turn them in.

00:16:42.020 --> 00:16:44.140
Roger that, Deputy!

00:16:44.140 --> 00:16:47.150
Takayama, will you really
be fine on your own?

00:16:47.150 --> 00:16:48.170
I will.

00:16:48.170 --> 00:16:51.360
And I need you to tell the conductor something for me, Koumi.

00:16:51.360 --> 00:16:54.030
Get him to make sure everyone's in their seats.

00:16:55.700 --> 00:16:58.450
I'll be right there once I detach the engines.

00:16:59.740 --> 00:17:00.580
Okay.

00:17:01.080 --> 00:17:01.950
Be careful.

00:17:05.040 --> 00:17:06.170
Come on, Sakurai.

00:17:07.460 --> 00:17:08.590
Sakurai?

00:17:11.260 --> 00:17:13.090
Count me in.

00:17:13.090 --> 00:17:14.090
What?!

00:17:14.380 --> 00:17:18.100
No way I can let you take all the glory.

00:17:23.480 --> 00:17:26.600
Now we just pull up this release lever!

00:17:26.600 --> 00:17:28.730
That'll disconnect the cars!

00:17:29.310 --> 00:17:31.980
We've gotta jump onto the generator car as soon as that happens!

00:17:32.440 --> 00:17:34.440
Or we'll just get further and further away!

00:17:34.440 --> 00:17:36.950
All right! Let's just get this over with!

00:17:36.950 --> 00:17:38.200
Okay, on three!

00:17:39.370 --> 00:17:40.700
One, two...

00:17:45.960 --> 00:17:47.620
Three! Okay!

00:17:47.620 --> 00:17:48.960
Sakurai, jump!

00:17:53.420 --> 00:17:55.220
What's the matter, Sakurai?

00:17:55.220 --> 00:17:58.220
Looks like I'm not so great after all.

00:17:58.220 --> 00:18:00.350
I hurt my leg in that firefight.

00:18:00.970 --> 00:18:02.640
You go first, Takayama.

00:18:02.640 --> 00:18:03.890
What?

00:18:05.680 --> 00:18:07.190
Hurry, you two!

00:18:08.520 --> 00:18:10.980
Takayama, what are you doing?!

00:18:12.320 --> 00:18:14.150
Takayama!

00:18:14.150 --> 00:18:15.240
Sakurai.

00:18:16.900 --> 00:18:18.860
I can't just leave you behind!

00:18:22.450 --> 00:18:26.200
Aoi! Takayama!

00:18:40.800 --> 00:18:43.390
You sure are a moron.

00:18:44.470 --> 00:18:46.350
I was just too scared to jump.

00:18:49.100 --> 00:18:52.110
I'm taking off my stockings.
You better not look.

00:18:52.110 --> 00:18:53.900
What? S-Sure.

00:19:01.740 --> 00:19:03.490
Y-You okay?

00:19:06.200 --> 00:19:07.580
Just fine!

00:19:07.580 --> 00:19:09.290
You look and you're dead!

00:19:11.000 --> 00:19:13.000
Wh-What?

00:19:13.960 --> 00:19:16.550
This has happened to us before, hasn't it?

00:19:17.340 --> 00:19:18.550
On the Ashio Line.

00:19:21.130 --> 00:19:22.550
Has it really?

00:19:31.520 --> 00:19:33.440
This is all I can do for now.

00:19:33.440 --> 00:19:36.150
D-Don't stare.

00:19:36.150 --> 00:19:38.940
I don't have pretty legs.

00:19:39.440 --> 00:19:40.950
You think?

00:19:40.950 --> 00:19:43.320
You're pretty enough to me, Sakurai.

00:20:00.420 --> 00:20:02.880
Reminds me of going
through the Usui Pass.

00:20:05.850 --> 00:20:07.010
Yeah, I remember.

00:20:08.600 --> 00:20:10.480
Hey, Takayama.

00:20:13.020 --> 00:20:14.020
I...

00:20:33.870 --> 00:20:35.080
Captain Gonou!

00:20:35.580 --> 00:20:37.630
We're gonna stop that train!

00:20:38.210 --> 00:20:39.800
Brace for impact!

00:20:45.390 --> 00:20:49.810
They're going <i>down</i> the up line, with three DF51s in tandem!

00:20:50.350 --> 00:20:51.350
I get it!

00:20:51.350 --> 00:20:54.440
There's a point up ahead where
the double-track section merges.

00:20:54.440 --> 00:20:56.560
They're trying to get ahead
of us before there!

00:20:56.560 --> 00:20:58.060
What are you babbling about?

00:20:58.060 --> 00:20:59.070
You wanna know?

00:20:59.820 --> 00:21:03.070
For a scaredy cat, you sure are...

00:21:05.660 --> 00:21:08.530
more scared than usual.

00:21:08.530 --> 00:21:11.410
I guess you wouldn't be you otherwise.

00:21:11.910 --> 00:21:13.830
But that's all right.

00:21:16.330 --> 00:21:19.710
I'll always protect you.

00:21:29.890 --> 00:21:31.890
Looks like we're saved.

00:21:31.890 --> 00:21:34.140
I'm starting to think
we're just really lucky.

00:21:36.600 --> 00:21:38.520
Oh, I'm so happy!

00:21:38.520 --> 00:21:40.110
Well, I'm not.

00:21:40.110 --> 00:21:41.150
Why?

00:21:42.030 --> 00:21:45.700
Why do I have to be subjected to being carried by a prince?

00:21:45.700 --> 00:21:46.990
A prince?

00:21:47.490 --> 00:21:48.370
Me?

00:21:59.500 --> 00:22:00.670
Takayama!

00:22:00.670 --> 00:22:01.710
Koumi!

00:22:01.710 --> 00:22:02.750
Takayama!

00:22:02.750 --> 00:22:03.920
Deputy!

00:22:03.920 --> 00:22:04.800
Iwaizumi!

00:22:04.800 --> 00:22:06.130
Aoi!

00:22:07.180 --> 00:22:09.430
Thank goodness!

00:23:40.980 --> 00:23:45.730
The JNR KiHa81 series is Japan's first express electric locomotive.

00:23:45.730 --> 00:23:49.190
It's also known as the Hatsukari,
the name of the first train it hauled.

00:23:49.190 --> 00:23:54.160
It inherits the characteristic hood design of the JNR 151 series thatвЂ”

00:23:54.160 --> 00:23:56.490
Sorry! That's not quite right.

00:23:57.120 --> 00:24:02.420
Next episode, Takayama and I are riding on a JNR KiHa381 series.

00:24:02.420 --> 00:24:06.250
The final episode of Rail Wars: Everyone's Waiting.

00:24:06.250 --> 00:24:08.840
Wait, what're you two doing all alone together?!
